# Coordinator source and receipt review

Reviewed ElementUtil.generateUUID source independently: fresh v4 is requested before all branches, root/member UUIDv5 paths remain source-specific, and null/unresolved getter observations are evaluated only when reached. Distinct selected semantic/resource identity roles and proposed atomic reservation are separated from upstream generation. The canonical-spelling and immutable-observation input restrictions do not claim full Java/EMF adapter compatibility.

All18 new domain cases plus28 existing regressions passed; one real selected JSON Document/Editor/immutable SnapshotStore save and fresh-store reload test passed. The initial integration lock refusal happened before tests, is retained with its original lock/runner, and was resolved by offline generation of the new harness lock only. All registry records remain unchanged; only inactive local packages/default workflow edges were pruned. Source/format/clippy checks pass for both suites.

The coordinator is distinct from the implementation worker and also executed captures; its only production contribution is the public module export. No second runtime executor, upstream runtime comparison, complete native adapter, crash-recovery or whole-area parity acceptance is claimed.
